'''Nobillians'''<ref name="ILM Discord">{{OfficialDiscord|discordname=.holocronkeeper|name=Leland Chee|servername=[[ILM Immersive]]|date=2022-11-28|messagelink=https://discord.com/channels/768613519774973963/768613519774973966/1046599042525843456|quote=For Last Call, we had come up with Nobillian for the species name of Neeva and her brother, Neevan.|archivefile=File:LelandChee-NobillianID-Discord.jpg}}</ref> were a species of [[insect]]oid beings found in [[the galaxy]].<ref name="TLJ" /> [[Neeva]] and [[Neevaan]] were two Nobillians that lived on [[Nar Shaddaa]] and were enemies of the criminal [[Boggs Triff]].<ref name="Last Call" /> Multiple members of the [[species]] attended the [[Canto Casino and Racetrack]] on [[Cantonica]]<ref name="TLJ" /> in [[34 ABY]].<ref name="34 ABY Date Note">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' places the events of [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']] in [[34 ABY]]. [[Star Wars: Episode VIII The Last Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VIII ''The Last Jedi'']] takes place immediately after the end of ''The Force Awakens''.</ref>

{{Species-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Nobillians, albeit unidentified, first appeared in the [[2017]] film [[Star Wars: Episode VIII The Last Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VIII ''The Last Jedi'']].<ref name="TLJ" /> Although still unidentified at the time, [[Lucasfilm Story Group]] member [[Pablo Hidalgo]] nicknamed the species Glambug.<ref name="Hidalgo">{{Twitter|pabl0hidalgo|status/1433860042046988289|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|date=2021-09-03|quote=The individual characters K007a and K007b have names in my notes, but no species name. I nicknamed her Glambug. :)|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/jUJjF|nolive=1}} {{C|In response to: "This alien I designed for #TheLastJedi showed up in the latest trailer for #GalaxysEdge VR experience. Does this species have a name yet? @pabl0hidalgo"}}</ref> In the official [[ILM Immersive]] [[Wikipedia:Discord|Discord]] server, the species was revealed to be named Nobillian by Lucasfilm Story Group member [[Leland Chee]].<ref name="ILM Discord" /> The species was named after [[Lillian Noble]] of [[Lucasfilm Publicity]] due to the work she did in the early story development of the [[2021]] VR [[Star Wars video games|video game]] ''[[Star Wars: Tales from the Galaxy's Edge – Last Call]]'' to make the character Neeva a more integral part of the game.<ref name="ILMX">{{ILMxLAB|url=news/beyond-the-spires-designing-the-bounty-of-boggs-triff|text=Beyond the Spires: Designing "The Bounty of Boggs Triff"}}</ref>

